==Tips==
* When combined with the [[Shark]] race, Mammoth is tremendously effective in hunting [[Sea Events]] because it enables the user to hold {{Ability|F}} move indefinitely until the enemy is defeated, although it is somewhat slow, and it possesses a huge risk against [[Terrorshark]]s and other dangerous sea events. However it is extremely effective against [[Sea Beast]]s. 
* Players should consider switching to Mammoth only when they reach or are close to reaching maximum [[Levels|Level]], as Mammoth has high mastery requirements.
* If the player has allocated their stats towards fruit-based attributes, they may find Mammoth suitable. However, if their stats are focused on Melee, Defense, and Sword, they should opt for other fruits instead.
* Similar to other transformation-based fruits, it disables the user's other weapons such as [[Fighting Style]], [[Sword]], and [[Gun]]. The user should activate their transformation prior to engaging in battles with [[Bosses]] or in PvP encounters.
* Mammoth is very good for farming when transformed because it enables the to hold {{Ability|F}} indefinitely and unlock {{Ability|TAP}}. Additionally, the fourth [M1] attack has a very good [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
* It is also recommend to turn off "Camera Shake" in the settings so the user can farm smoothly.

==Trivia==
* The impact from jumping works the opposite way from Awakened [[Buddha]]. Buddha's jump damage applies on the initial jump from the ground, as for Mammoth, it applies on its landing. The impact from jumping can reset air jumps. This can be useful in evading water for players not of the [[Shark]] race by touching the surface of the water to reset air jumps while taking little to no damage. 
* The {{Ability|Twin Hooks|X}} move on [[Twin Hooks]], parallels the {{Ability|X}} move on Mammoth.
* If the player pairs [[Bear Ears]] and [[Shark]] race with Mammoth, their damage reduction will be increased from 50 to about 70%. With [[Water Body]], the player's damage reduction will increase from about 70% to about 80% due to [[Water Body]] boosting their defense by 65% for 4.5 seconds. (Recommended to get [[Race Awakening]] due to [[Shark]] V3 being heavily nerfed)
* If the player pairs [[Bear Ears]] and [[Cyborg (race)|Cyborg]] race (V2 and above) with Mammoth, its passive damage reduction will be raised from 55% to about 62% for any attack, and for attacks by Melee, Sword or Gun the player will have 85.5%. With the [T] ability active, the player will have ~69% in any attack and for attacks by Melee, Sword and Gun the player will have ~72%.
* Mammoth is one of two pairs of fruits to share the same monetary value. The other pairs are, [[Yeti]] and [[Tiger]] at {{Money|5,000,000}} or {{Robux|3000}}. 
** (Shared with [[T-Rex]] at {{Money|2,700,000}} or {{Robux|2,350}})
* Mammoth is the third fruit that doesn't need a [[Fury Meter]] to transform. (The first being [[Phoenix]], second being [[Tiger]], fourth being [[Yeti]])
* When getting hit by a move that has a grabbing animation while transformed, such as [[Dragon]] {{Ability|Dragon|X}}, the user will fly in weird ways that should be normal when at the size of a regular player, making it look comical in some sorts. 
* Mammoth's fruit model is completely different to its icon and transformation, while the former wears a purple cloth lined with gold and blue spikes, the latter wears dark armor plates with blue/red spikes.  
* Defeating the Youtuber [https://www.youtube.com/@Senpirates Senpirates] will earn the player the [[Titles|title]] "'''Mammoth Fan Club'''"  
* Mammoth is considered to be [[T-Rex]]'s rival.  
** Despite being the slower 'tank' variant between the two, Mammoth only has 7% more defense over its counterpart, while also lacking a Passive Ability, no '''[M1]''' untransformed, and overall much weaker offensive-attacks.

